{"name":"There Is Light","hex":"#002288","fetched":"2026-10-16","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"there","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adverb","definitions":["In or at a place or location (stated, implied or otherwise indicated) that is perceived to be away from, or at a relative distance from, the speaker (compare here).","At that point, stage, etc., visualised as a distinct place."]},{"part":"Interjection","definitions":["Used to offer encouragement or sympathy; see also there, there and there now.","Used to express victory or completion."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/there"},{"term":"light","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Electromagnetic radiation in the wavelength range visible to the human eye (about 400–750 nanometers): visible light.","Electromagnetic radiation in the wavelength range visible to the human eye or in nearby ranges (infrared or ultraviolet radiation)."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To start (a fire).","To set fire to; to set burning."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/light"}],"entries":[{"title":"There Is","blocks":[{"text":"\"There Is\" is the second and final single from Box Car Racer's eponymous album. The single peaked at number 32 on the Billboard's Modern Rock Tracks chart."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/3/3a/Box_Car_Racer_single_cover_There_Is.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/There_Is"},{"title":"Light","blocks":[{"text":"Light, visible light, or visible radiation is electromagnetic radiation that can be perceived by the human eye. Visible light spans the visible spectrum and is usually defined as having wavelengths in the range of 400–700 nanometers (nm), corresponding to frequencies of 750–420 terahertz. The visible band sits adjacent to the infrared and the ultraviolet, called collectively optical radiation."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fa/Pris